\mt1 THE REVELATION OF ST. JOHN THE DIVINE  
\c 12  
\p
\v 1 \w And\w* there \w appeared\w* a \w great\w* \w wonder\w* \w in\w* \w heaven\w*; a \w woman\w* clothed \w with\w* the \w sun\w*, \w and\w* the \w moon\w* \w under\w* \w her\w* \w feet\w*, \w and\w* \w upon\w* \w her\w* \w head\w* a \w crown\w* of \w twelve\w* \w stars\w*:  
\v 2 \w And\w* she \w being\w* \w with\w* \w child\w* \w cried\w*, travailing in \w birth\w*, \w and\w* \w pained\w* to be \w delivered\w*.  
\v 3 \w And\w* there \w appeared\w* \w another\w* \w wonder\w* \w in\w* \w heaven\w*; \w and\w* \w behold\w* a \w great\w* \w red\w* \w dragon\w*, \w having\w* \w seven\w* \w heads\w* \w and\w* \w ten\w* \w horns\w*, \w and\w* \w seven\w* \w crowns\w* \w upon\w* \w his\w* \w heads\w*.  
\v 4 \w And\w* \w his\w* \w tail\w* \w drew\w* the third \w part\w* of the \w stars\w* of \w heaven\w*, \w and\w* did \w cast\w* \w them\w* \w to\w* the \w earth\w*: \w and\w* the \w dragon\w* \w stood\w* \w before\w* the \w woman\w* which was \w ready\w* to be \w delivered\w*, \w for\w* to \w devour\w* \w her\w* \w child\w* as soon \w as\w* it was \w born\w*.  
\v 5 \w And\w* she brought \w forth\w* a \w man\w* \w child\w*, \w who\w* was \w to\w* \w rule\w* \w all\w* \w nations\w* \w with\w* a \w rod\w* of \w iron\w*: \w and\w* \w her\w* \w child\w* was caught \w up\w* \w unto\w* \w God\w*, \w and\w* \add to\add* \w his\w* \w throne\w*.  
\v 6 \w And\w* the \w woman\w* \w fled\w* \w into\w* the \w wilderness\w*, \w where\w* she \w hath\w* a \w place\w* \w prepared\w* \w of\w* \w God\w*, \w that\w* they should \w feed\w* \w her\w* \w there\w* a \w thousand\w* two \w hundred\w* \add and\add* \w threescore\w* \w days\w*.  
\v 7 \w And\w* there \w was\w* \w war\w* \w in\w* \w heaven\w*: \w Michael\w* \w and\w* \w his\w* \w angels\w* \w fought\w* \w against\w* the \w dragon\w*; \w and\w* the \w dragon\w* \w fought\w* \w and\w* \w his\w* \w angels\w*,  
\v 8 \w And\w* \w prevailed\w* \w not\w*; \w neither\w* \w was\w* \w their\w* \w place\w* \w found\w* any \w more\w* \w in\w* \w heaven\w*.  
\v 9 \w And\w* the \w great\w* \w dragon\w* was cast \w out\w*, that \w old\w* \w serpent\w*, \w called\w* the \w Devil\w*, \w and\w* \w Satan\w*, which \w deceiveth\w* the \w whole\w* \w world\w*: he was cast \w out\w* \w into\w* the \w earth\w*, \w and\w* \w his\w* \w angels\w* were cast \w out\w* \w with\w* \w him\w*.  
\v 10 \w And\w* I \w heard\w* a \w loud\w* \w voice\w* \w saying\w* \w in\w* \w heaven\w*, \w Now\w* is \w come\w* \w salvation\w*, \w and\w* \w strength\w*, \w and\w* the \w kingdom\w* of \w our\w* \w God\w*, \w and\w* the \w power\w* of \w his\w* \w Christ\w*: \w for\w* the \w accuser\w* of \w our\w* \w brethren\w* is cast \w down\w*, \w which\w* \w accused\w* \w them\w* \w before\w* \w our\w* \w God\w* \w day\w* \w and\w* \w night\w*.  
\v 11 \w And\w* \w they\w* \w overcame\w* \w him\w* \w by\w* the \w blood\w* of the \w Lamb\w*, \w and\w* \w by\w* the \w word\w* of \w their\w* \w testimony\w*; \w and\w* they \w loved\w* \w not\w* \w their\w* \w lives\w* \w unto\w* the \w death\w*.  
\v 12 \w Therefore\w* \w rejoice\w*, \add ye\add* \w heavens\w*, \w and\w* \w ye\w* that \w dwell\w* \w in\w* \w them\w*. \w Woe\w* to the \w inhabiters\w* of the \w earth\w* \w and\w* of the \w sea\w*! \w for\w* the \w devil\w* is come \w down\w* \w unto\w* \w you\w*, \w having\w* \w great\w* \w wrath\w*, \w because\w* he knoweth \w that\w* he \w hath\w* but a \w short\w* \w time\w*.  
\v 13 \w And\w* \w when\w* the \w dragon\w* \w saw\w* \w that\w* he was \w cast\w* \w unto\w* the \w earth\w*, he \w persecuted\w* the \w woman\w* \w which\w* brought \w forth\w* the \w man\w* \add child\add*.  
\v 14 \w And\w* to the \w woman\w* were \w given\w* \w two\w* \w wings\w* of a \w great\w* \w eagle\w*, \w that\w* she might \w fly\w* \w into\w* the \w wilderness\w*, \w into\w* \w her\w* \w place\w*, \w where\w* she is \w nourished\w* \w for\w* a \w time\w*, \w and\w* \w times\w*, \w and\w* \w half\w* a \w time\w*, \w from\w* the \w face\w* of the \w serpent\w*.  
\v 15 \w And\w* the \w serpent\w* cast \w out\w* \w of\w* \w his\w* \w mouth\w* \w water\w* \w as\w* a \w flood\w* \w after\w* the \w woman\w*, \w that\w* he might \w cause\w* \w her\w* to be carried away of the \w flood\w*.  
\v 16 \w And\w* the \w earth\w* \w helped\w* the \w woman\w*, \w and\w* the \w earth\w* \w opened\w* \w her\w* \w mouth\w*, \w and\w* swallowed \w up\w* the \w flood\w* \w which\w* the \w dragon\w* cast \w out\w* \w of\w* \w his\w* \w mouth\w*.  
\v 17 \w And\w* the \w dragon\w* was \w wroth\w* \w with\w* the \w woman\w*, \w and\w* \w went\w* to \w make\w* \w war\w* \w with\w* the \w remnant\w* of \w her\w* \w seed\w*, \w which\w* \w keep\w* the \w commandments\w* of \w God\w*, \w and\w* \w have\w* the \w testimony\w* of \w Jesus\w* \w Christ\w*.   
\c 13  
\p
\v 1 \w And\w* I \w stood\w* \w upon\w* the \w sand\w* of the \w sea\w*, \w and\w* \w saw\w* a \w beast\w* rise \w up\w* out \w of\w* the \w sea\w*, \w having\w* \w seven\w* \w heads\w* \w and\w* \w ten\w* \w horns\w*, \w and\w* \w upon\w* \w his\w* \w horns\w* \w ten\w* \w crowns\w*, \w and\w* \w upon\w* \w his\w* \w heads\w* the \w name\w* of \w blasphemy\w*.  
\v 2 \w And\w* the \w beast\w* \w which\w* I \w saw\w* \w was\w* like \w unto\w* a \w leopard\w*, \w and\w* \w his\w* \w feet\w* were \w as\w* \add the feet\add* of a \w bear\w*, \w and\w* \w his\w* \w mouth\w* \w as\w* the \w mouth\w* of a \w lion\w*: \w and\w* the \w dragon\w* \w gave\w* \w him\w* \w his\w* \w power\w*, \w and\w* \w his\w* \w seat\w*, \w and\w* \w great\w* \w authority\w*.  
\v 3 \w And\w* I \w saw\w* \w one\w* of \w his\w* \w heads\w* as it \w were\w* \w wounded\w* \w to\w* \w death\w*; \w and\w* \w his\w* \w deadly\w* \w wound\w* was \w healed\w*: \w and\w* \w all\w* the \w world\w* \w wondered\w* \w after\w* the \w beast\w*.  
\v 4 \w And\w* they \w worshipped\w* the \w dragon\w* \w which\w* \w gave\w* \w power\w* unto the \w beast\w*: \w and\w* they \w worshipped\w* the \w beast\w*, \w saying\w*, \w Who\w* \add is\add* like \w unto\w* the \w beast\w*? \w who\w* is \w able\w* to make \w war\w* \w with\w* \w him\w*?  
\v 5 \w And\w* there was \w given\w* unto \w him\w* a \w mouth\w* \w speaking\w* great \w things\w* \w and\w* \w blasphemies\w*; \w and\w* \w power\w* was \w given\w* unto \w him\w* to \w continue\w* \w forty\w* \add and\add* \w two\w* \w months\w*.  
\v 6 \w And\w* he \w opened\w* \w his\w* \w mouth\w* \w in\w* \w blasphemy\w* \w against\w* \w God\w*, to \w blaspheme\w* \w his\w* \w name\w*, \w and\w* \w his\w* \w tabernacle\w*, \w and\w* \w them\w* that \w dwell\w* \w in\w* \w heaven\w*.  
\v 7 \w And\w* it was \w given\w* unto \w him\w* to \w make\w* \w war\w* \w with\w* the \w saints\w*, \w and\w* to \w overcome\w* \w them\w*: \w and\w* \w power\w* was \w given\w* \w him\w* \w over\w* \w all\w* \w kindreds\w*, \w and\w* \w tongues\w*, \w and\w* \w nations\w*.  
\v 8 \w And\w* \w all\w* \w that\w* \w dwell\w* \w upon\w* the \w earth\w* shall \w worship\w* \w him\w*, \w whose\w* \w names\w* \w are\w* \w not\w* \w written\w* \w in\w* the \w book\w* of \w life\w* of the \w Lamb\w* \w slain\w* \w from\w* the \w foundation\w* of the \w world\w*.  
\v 9 \w If\w* any \w man\w* \w have\w* an \w ear\w*, let him \w hear\w*.  
\v 10 \w He\w* \w that\w* leadeth \w into\w* \w captivity\w* shall \w go\w* \w into\w* \w captivity\w*: \w he\w* \w that\w* \w killeth\w* \w with\w* the \w sword\w* \w must\w* \w be\w* \w killed\w* \w with\w* the \w sword\w*. \w Here\w* \w is\w* the \w patience\w* \w and\w* the \w faith\w* of the \w saints\w*.  
\v 11 \w And\w* I \w beheld\w* \w another\w* \w beast\w* coming \w up\w* out \w of\w* the \w earth\w*; \w and\w* he \w had\w* \w two\w* \w horns\w* \w like\w* a \w lamb\w*, \w and\w* he \w spake\w* \w as\w* a \w dragon\w*.  
\v 12 \w And\w* he \w exerciseth\w* \w all\w* the \w power\w* of the \w first\w* \w beast\w* \w before\w* \w him\w*, \w and\w* \w causeth\w* the \w earth\w* \w and\w* \w them\w* which \w dwell\w* \w therein\w* \w to\w* \w worship\w* the \w first\w* \w beast\w*, \w whose\w* \w deadly\w* \w wound\w* was \w healed\w*.  
\v 13 \w And\w* he \w doeth\w* \w great\w* \w wonders\w*, \w so\w* \w that\w* he \w maketh\w* \w fire\w* come \w down\w* \w from\w* \w heaven\w* \w on\w* the \w earth\w* in the \w sight\w* of \w men\w*,  
\v 14 \w And\w* \w deceiveth\w* \w them\w* that \w dwell\w* \w on\w* the \w earth\w* \w by\w* \add the means of\add* \w those\w* \w miracles\w* \w which\w* \w he\w* had \w power\w* to \w do\w* in the sight \w of\w* the \w beast\w*; \w saying\w* to \w them\w* that \w dwell\w* \w on\w* the \w earth\w*, that they should \w make\w* an \w image\w* to the \w beast\w*, \w which\w* \w had\w* the \w wound\w* by a \w sword\w*, \w and\w* did \w live\w*.  
\v 15 \w And\w* \w he\w* had \w power\w* to \w give\w* \w life\w* unto the \w image\w* of the \w beast\w*, \w that\w* the \w image\w* of the \w beast\w* \w should\w* \w both\w* \w speak\w*, \w and\w* \w cause\w* \w that\w* as \w many\w* \w as\w* \w would\w* \w not\w* \w worship\w* the \w image\w* of the \w beast\w* should be \w killed\w*.  
\v 16 \w And\w* he \w causeth\w* \w all\w*, \w both\w* \w small\w* \w and\w* \w great\w*, \w rich\w* \w and\w* \w poor\w*, \w free\w* \w and\w* \w bond\w*, \w to\w* \w receive\w* a \w mark\w* \w in\w* \w their\w* \w right\w* \w hand\w*, \w or\w* \w in\w* \w their\w* \w foreheads\w*:  
\v 17 \w And\w* \w that\w* \w no\w* \w man\w* \w might\w* \w buy\w* \w or\w* \w sell\w*, save \w he\w* \w that\w* \w had\w* the \w mark\w*, \w or\w* the \w name\w* of the \w beast\w*, \w or\w* the \w number\w* of \w his\w* \w name\w*.  
\v 18 \w Here\w* \w is\w* \w wisdom\w*. Let \w him\w* that \w hath\w* \w understanding\w* \w count\w* the \w number\w* of the \w beast\w*: \w for\w* it \w is\w* the \w number\w* of a \w man\w*; \w and\w* \w his\w* \w number\w* \add is\add* Six hundred \w threescore\w* \add and\add* \w six\w*.
